# Invented dialogue long enough to cancel part-way through a paced transcription.
T: Welcome back. Let us start by checking in on how you are feeling today.
C: I am feeling steady today. Last week was busier than I expected.
T: Tell me about the busiest part of the week.
C: There was a deadline at the community garden, where I volunteer on Tuesdays.
T: And how did you handle the pressure of that deadline?
C: I made a list, did one thing at a time, and took short breaks to stretch.
T: That is a skill worth noticing. What helped you stay with the list?
C: Knowing that the garden matters to me. It made the effort feel worthwhile.
T: Let us think about where else that sense of purpose might help.
C: Perhaps with the cooking course I have been putting off since spring.
